From 4c2d9f10a6a42caf9663dc145d3744c9d9894194 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:57:17 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: take only a subscriber's refusal from a ubus notify
 response

With notify_response set (usteer sets it), hostapd sends each probe,
authentication and association as a ubus notify, waits for the
subscribers' status codes, and refuses the client with that code when
it is not 0. ubus_event_cb() stored every subscriber's code over the
previous one, so the last subscriber to answer decided. A refusal from
one subscriber was lost when another answered 0. A subscriber with no
opinion also refused the client: a ucode subscriber whose handler
returns nothing answers UBUS_STATUS_NO_DATA, one with no notify handler
UBUS_STATUS_METHOD_NOT_FOUND, and hostapd used those as 802.11 status
codes. On the BSS Transition Management query path the same codes made
hostapd leave the answer to a subscriber that never sent one.

Keep the first nonzero code, and treat NO_DATA and METHOD_NOT_FOUND as
no opinion. Neither is a status code a subscriber would return for a
refusal; both are what ubus answers for a subscriber that does not
handle the notification.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile          |  2 +-
 package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c | 12 +++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
index ce8ceb25b8..b46d451ffc 100644
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/Makefile
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=hostapd
-PKG_RELEASE:=7
+PKG_RELEASE:=8
 
 PKG_SOURCE_URL:=https://w1.fi/hostap.git
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
diff --git a/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c b/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c
index 0fc1c6d8e7..89c5ed9cce 100644
--- a/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c
+++ b/package/network/services/hostapd/src/src/ap/ubus.c
@@ -3076,7 +3076,17 @@ ubus_event_cb(struct ubus_notify_request *req, int idx, int ret)
 {
 	struct ubus_event_req *ureq = container_of(req, struct ubus_event_req, nreq);
 
-	ureq->resp = ret;
+	/*
+	 * A subscriber that does not handle the notification has no say:
+	 * ubus answers NO_DATA for a handler that returned nothing and
+	 * METHOD_NOT_FOUND for one without a notify handler. Of the others,
+	 * the first refusal stands; a later 0 does not undo it.
+	 */
+	if (ret == UBUS_STATUS_NO_DATA || ret == UBUS_STATUS_METHOD_NOT_FOUND)
+		return;
+
+	if (!ureq->resp)
+		ureq->resp = ret;
 }
 
 int hostapd_ubus_handle_event(struct hostapd_data *hapd, struct hostapd_ubus_request *req)
